# global-monorepo-packages

> **Purpose:** Keep the monorepo clean and the shared contract in one place.
>
> **Applies to:** Every file in the repo (always on).

## Package manager
- Use pnpm only. Never use npm or yarn.
- Add a dependency with `pnpm --filter <workspace> add <pkg>`.
- Add a new dependency only with a one-line reason in the commit message.

## Workspaces
- Apps: `apps/web`, `apps/api`. Packages: `@stamp/schema`, `@stamp/typescript-config`, `@stamp/eslint-config`.
- Link packages with `"workspace:*"`.
- Create a new package only if 2 or more workspaces import it.

## Shared contract
- Guide, Claim, API bodies and stream events are defined once, in `@stamp/schema`.
- Never redefine a shared type inside an app. Import it.
- A change to `@stamp/schema` must build and pass tests in both apps.

## Turbo
- Packages build before apps (`build` depends on `^build`).
- Run tasks from the root: `pnpm dev`, `pnpm build`, `pnpm test`, `pnpm lint`.
